  "The hotline has also revealed important trends in mental health needs across the country, including the high prevalence of gender-based violence-related trauma, youth mental health crises, and the impact of economic hardship on mental wellbeing.": "copy.a40ee93d9e5979f8",
  "Youth Art Therapy Program Expands to 5 New Provinces": "copy.670810b39800cbc2",
  "15 Apr 2025": "copy.50f9766d350de310",
  "Creative expression through art therapy is helping at-risk youth process trauma and build resilience, with the program now serving over 2,000 young people.": "copy.003d69115fb8a927",
  "World Changers MHC Org's Youth Art Therapy Program has expanded to five new provinces, bringing the total to seven provinces served across South Africa. The program, which uses creative expression as a therapeutic tool, now serves over 2,000 young people aged 10-24. The program offers a variety of creative modalities, including visual arts, music therapy, drama, dance, and creative writing. Trained art therapists work with young people in schools, community centres, and residential care facilities to help them process trauma, express emotions, and build resilience. Participants in the program have shown significant improvements in emotional regulation, self-esteem, and social skills. Many have also shown improvements in academic performance and reduced involvement in risky behaviours. The expansion was made possible through partnerships with provincial departments of education and social development, corporate sponsors, and international development organisations. Plans for 2026 include extending the program to the remaining two provinces and developing an online component for young people in remote areas.": "copy.7f8837e85021c698",
  "World Changers MHC Org's Youth Art Therapy Program has expanded to five new provinces, bringing the total to seven provinces served across South Africa. The program, which uses creative expression as a therapeutic tool, now serves over 2,000 young people aged 10-24.": "copy.e55d80e8aeb22403",
  "The program offers a variety of creative modalities, including visual arts, music therapy, drama, dance, and creative writing. Trained art therapists work with young people in schools, community centres, and residential care facilities to help them process trauma, express emotions, and build resilience.": "copy.09744112d41312b3",
  "Participants in the program have shown significant improvements in emotional regulation, self-esteem, and social skills. Many have also shown improvements in academic performance and reduced involvement in risky behaviours.": "copy.6e8d961b09bb601a",
  "The expansion was made possible through partnerships with provincial departments of education and social development, corporate sponsors, and international development organisations. Plans for 2026 include extending the program to the remaining two provinces and developing an online component for young people in remote areas.": "copy.0f1f4f888979ff87",
  "Disaster Relief: Rapid Response to KZN Flooding": "copy.86ed2799114003db",
  "28 Mar 2025": "copy.51354d2a5aa74fd5",
  "Disaster Relief": "copy.d194aafcc4bbb91f",
  "Our humanitarian response team deployed within 24 hours, providing emergency shelter, food, and psychological support to over 800 affected families.": "copy.37dfbb5c81ecfe37",
  "When devastating floods struck KwaZulu-Natal, World Changers MHC Org's humanitarian response team was on the ground within 24 hours, providing emergency assistance to affected communities. The response team, comprising social workers, counsellors, logistics coordinators, and volunteer emergency responders, provided a comprehensive range of services including emergency shelter, food parcels, clean water, clothing, and essential hygiene supplies to over 800 families. Critically, the response also included psychological first aid and ongoing mental health support for flood survivors, many of whom experienced significant trauma from the disaster. Counsellors worked in evacuation centres, providing individual and group support, and identifying individuals who needed referral for more intensive mental health services. The response highlighted the importance of integrating mental health support into disaster relief operations — an approach that World Changers has championed and that is increasingly being adopted by humanitarian organisations globally. In the weeks following the initial response, the organisation established semi-permanent support centres in the most affected communities, providing ongoing counselling, community rebuilding activities, and advocacy for the mental health needs of disaster survivors.": "copy.37ac6b8568173609",
  "When devastating floods struck KwaZulu-Natal, World Changers MHC Org's humanitarian response team was on the ground within 24 hours, providing emergency assistance to affected communities.": "copy.c2fa0090fd78b489",
